-- title:
--   Hecke operators killing the new lattice kill the new subspace
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, $q$ a prime, and let $A$ be an Atkin–Lehner datum for $(M,q)$, that is, a natural number $R = A.R$ with $M = qR$ together with integers $a, b$ satisfying $qa - Rb = 1$. Let $t$ belong to [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ M}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$ (the prescribed excluded set $\{\ell : \ell \mid M\}$ removes all the $U$-generators, so the algebra is the anemic one). Assume that $t$ annihilates every element of [`CuspForm.newLattice A hq`](def/CuspForm_NewLattice.html#L16), the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of those $g \in S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ such that for every $s$ in that Hecke algebra the form $s g$ lies in [`CuspForm.intLattice M 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of the weight-$2$ forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers) and satisfies $\operatorname{Tr}(s g) = 0$ and $\operatorname{Tr}(w_A(s g)) = 0$; here $\operatorname{Tr} =$ [`CuspForm.traceLin A hq`](def/CuspForm_LevelLoweringTrace.html#L18) is the map $S_2(\Gamma_0(M)) \to S_2(\Gamma_0(R))$ sending $h \mapsto h + U_q(h \mid_2 W_A)$, and $w_A =$ [`CuspForm.atkinLehnerLin A 2`](def/CuspForm_AtkinLehnerOperator.html#L41) is $h \mapsto h \mid_2 W_A$. Then for every $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ with $\operatorname{Tr} f = 0$ and $\operatorname{Tr}(w_A f) = 0$ one has $t f = 0$.
--
--   The $q$-new subspace of $S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ is realised here as the common kernel of the two level-lowering traces from level $M = qR$ to level $R$, and the new lattice is its integral avatar; the statement says that the anemic Hecke algebra acts on the new subspace through the quotient that acts faithfully on the new lattice, because the traces and the Atkin–Lehner involution preserve rationality of $q$-expansions. It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeWordHom_eq_zero_of_forall_newLattice`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeWordHom_eq_zero_of_forall_newLattice) in the level-lowering part of the argument.
-- source:
